* ''The system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Only each Nexus's Kahu cabal writes the house canon live (`lares`, `lararium` and every disk-sourced holding but the board; 2026-11-11 below). Every other wiki, and every other hand, mounts them read-only by CID: the latest release that cabal approved. The release rides the Nexus's crossroads board as its public answer, naming the floor CID under the Kahu steward's seal. The cabal approves the exact bytes under its charter's threshold, and a herm carries the answer without signing it. Every wiki mounts that floor through `@oracle`, which never writes. A vessel moves its floor pin only when it accepts a newer signed release. With no Nexus speaking, it stands on its last accepted floor, or on genesis. The VESSEL pins the floor, one pin per (vessel, Nexus) (2026-11-11 below), so one vessel may hold two Nexuses' floors, and a face switch moves no floor. An edit aimed at the floor copies up into the wiki's own working layer, and an offering back rests as a signed entry on the Nexus's offer table beside the cabal's realm, never in it, where the steward's hand promotes it (the house's decision, 2026-11-13, overrulable: the road takes the built door's form, since realm drafts would seat the offerer inside the Kahu realm; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/offering#/the-canon-offer`>>). A lone hearth is a Nexus of one, so its operator stands as its own Kahu. Item `W26` carries the build.

